Mint-YT-Factory production log — 2026-08-27

This file preserves the user-provided GitHub Actions production log from the Kokoro migration/debugging run.

Key run milestones:
- Pipeline started successfully on Python 3.11.16.
- Gemini script model: gemini-flash-lite-latest.
- Visual/Search Director: Gemini.
- Stock media priority: Pexels VIDEO → Pixabay VIDEO → Pexels PHOTO → Pixabay PHOTO.
- Visual verification enabled; threshold 7.5/10.
- Story target: TTS-authoritative 35–43.9 seconds.
- Continuation: one locked next topic, final sentence only.
- Current topic: Why popcorn kernels explode.
- Gemini generated and accepted next topic: Why dry noodles snap into three.
- Kokoro TTS successfully loaded Kokoro-82M locally with voice af_heart, language a.
- Kokoro uses a single continuous narration pass; chunking disabled.
- Kokoro synthesis succeeded at 24 kHz.
- Adaptive narration speed was used to fit the target duration.
- SFX generation completed with 19 assets and mandatory FAAA reaction placement.
- Background music selected successfully.

Important failures observed during this run:
1. Before Kokoro migration, keyless TikTok TTS failed across all configured backends after 4 attempts.
2. After Kokoro migration, MoviePy failed because the generated raw WAV reported a shorter file duration than the processed clip requested. Error example: accessing t≈37.36–37.40s while clip duration was reported as 37s.
3. A subsequent attempt exposed a MoviePy frame-rate/array issue in the speed-adjustment path: ValueError: The truth value of an array with more than one element is ambiguous. Use a.any() or a.all().
4. An assembly contract mismatch was previously identified: the pipeline generated 14 image groups (7 scenes × 2 shots), while assemble.py expected 7. The contract was changed to expect 14.
5. Gemini visual verification sometimes temporarily failed; the stock pipeline then used conservative metadata fallback/provider fallback rather than unrelated media.
6. Gemini topic generation can produce invalid candidates; the continuation pipeline should retry Gemini rather than inject a static hard-coded topic.

Architecture/decisions captured by this log:
- Work directly on main and the publish-short workflow; do not create additional branches/workflows.
- Gemini must generate the seamless next-topic preview. Do not use a hard-coded recurring topic such as “Why onions make you cry” as a fallback.
- The accepted Gemini next topic is canonical and should be persisted for the next Short.
- Scene 7 should contain the seamless continuation preview as the final sentence only.
- Descriptions should describe the current Short’s topic, not the upcoming topic.
- Visuals should closely match the exact narration beat; unrelated/general scientific imagery is not acceptable.
- Script tone should be entertainment-first, fun, quirky, conversational, and low-jargon rather than dry/scientific.

Full user-supplied log is preserved in the conversation that requested this repository log entry.
